function chapterFive(){app.innerHTML=wrap(`<div class="topline chapter-nav"><button class="button ghost" onclick="map()">← Case map</button><span class="small">Chapter 5 of 8</span></div><article class="card chapter original"><p class="location">📍 20 Williams Street</p><p>Good job completing Chapter 4 and welcome to Chapter 5!</p><h3>The Second Town Hall</h3><p>You arrive at 20 Williams Street, a Colonial Revival building that served as Longmeadow’s Town Hall before the move to Greenwood Center. The town’s civic hubs have a habit of shifting: early meetings took place on the Green in 1716, the first municipal office opened at 417 Longmeadow Street in 1905, the town moved here in 1930, and it moved again to Greenwood Center in late 2024.</p><p>The thief is nowhere to be found. As you sit on the bench, you notice a slip of paper wedged into its frame. A new puzzle awaits.</p><section class="gallery"><figure><img src="asset-original-assets-chapter-5-1.jpg" alt="Map to 20 Williams Street"><figcaption>Map to 20 Williams Street</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="asset-original-assets-chapter-5-4.jpg" alt="20 Williams Street"><figcaption>20 Williams Street</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="asset-original-assets-chapter-5-3.jpg" alt="The clue left by the thief"><figcaption>The clue left by the thief</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="asset-original-assets-chapter-5-6.jpg" alt="The scroll pediment"><figcaption>The scroll pediment at 20 Williams Street</figcaption></figure></section><section class="answer"><h3>Did you solve the puzzle?</h3><button class="button full" onclick="submitAnswer(4)">Yes — submit our answer</button>${hintPanel(4)}</section></article>`) }
